    <wuid>7c01cf97:1380ef657a5:-79de</wuid>
    <transparent>true</transparent>
    <auto_size>false</auto_size>
    <text>Measurement of Ibeam(mA) by a calorimetric method :

We measure the power dissipated by the beam in LEBT Faraday Cup or in the Beam Stopper.

Acquisition :  Temp of Input water ( in the Faraday cup circuit.
                     Temp of Output water ( in the FC and the BS).
                      High Voltage 
                      Duty Cycle (1 if CW)


The water flow is constant ( 40 l/mn )

The formula to calculate Ibeam is :
    

     (((40/60) * 4186,8 * DeltaT) / Vht) * DutyCycle
        
Duty Cycle = 1 if CW mode

Signal    |   K633   |  ICV150l
--------------------------------------
GE            K633_1   channel 6    with threshold Relay
FC_IN       K633_2   channel 0
FC_OUT   K633_3   channel 1
IC_IN        K633_5   channel 4      Not Used
IC_OUT    K633-6   channel 5      Not Used
BS_IN       K633_7   channel 3   (----   IC_OUT  -----)
BS_OUT   K633_8   channel 2

FGA                        channel 7</text>
